Z||000000||Sevaan||06-28-2001||05:44 PM||||Okay, let's say you hypothetically have a Silver 1986 2m4. It's not in the best condition, it's not in the worst condition. Everything is stock. Inside are some nice blue seat covers (blue looks good with silver). Couple scratches on the outside paint, but overall everything looks pretty good.<P>You feel like spending CAN$100 (More or less) on the car this week. What do you do?<P>WHAT DO YOU DO?!<P>You can do anything you like. Paint the interior, add parts. Whatever.<P>The gauntlet has been thrown down! Winner gets the knowledge of knowing he helped contribute to the hypothetical vehicle!<P>And I'll hypothetically take some pictures of the process for you all.<P>- Sevaan<BR>- Silver 1986 2m4 (Hypothetical)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||06-28-2001||06:21 PM||||1) Buy three raffle tickets for the 88 GT T-top.<BR>2) Buy 10 pine tree air fresheners and a box of donuts.<BR>3) New plugs, cap, rotor, air filter, oil filter, oil.<BR>4) Get it professionaly detailed.<BR>5) Fiero Store glovebox.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||06-28-2001||06:22 PM||||what I would do first is a break upgrade and add a rear sway bar. (Control and breaking is essential) Next I would work on getting the AirCo charged. <P>------------------<BR>My Dream Fiero, you ask?<BR>That would be a automatic '86 or newer V6 GT Fastback with T-Tops and A/C, fully running and for sale for under $1000 CAN. Know someone who's selling a car like this for this price in the Toronto area? PLEASE E-MAIL ME!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||1
